  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. A long session (WBS 8.5) of 52 inputs with one fight, against a single suit of animated armour from input 30, which is not a combatant until then. Wren is a caster with 2 spell slots: Cure Wounds at input 37 spends the first and input 47 the second, so she ends the session with none. The Grey Lady is an NPC with a relationship only, not a combatant, and she cannot be attacked. Candles are the numeric thread: 3 at the start, burned at inputs 3, 19 and 29, so input 49 should find none. The holy water at input 38 has no mechanical effect on the already-fallen armour, and narration of it doing damage or healing is a CONTRADICT divergence. The iron key is gained at input 18 and left in the lock at input 21; the locket is gained at input 23 and given up at input 40. Three quests: the Grey Lady's rest runs to stage 3 and completes, the locked study runs to its max_stage 2 and completes, and Tobin's dog fails at input 27; input 48 asks about the dog afterwards. Three NPCs: Mrs Hale goes up twice from unfriendly to friendly, the Grey Lady up twice to allied, and Tobin down once to neutral and is never won back, so input 45 should not find him warm. The study door at input 15 (strength, DC 16) usually fails, and the key is the intended way in. The night's sleep at input 50 restores nothing (no rests). Inputs 30 to 36 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
}
